Changelog: 01-11-2026 11:22:09

Added. sFTP Tools (apps/sftp, package sftp_tools, Utilities; owner, 01-11-2026): the BC250 Bazzite Suite's SFTP Tools
made for the handheld, on the portable window. Its SFTP Client is four cards and its Server Manager a fifth, on one
connection: Connection (a row a field, each field on a page of its own with the touch keyboard on R3 and X Paste;
the key stepped through those in %USERPROFILE%\.ssh; X connects, a new server's key shown as ssh shows it and trusted
on X again into %USERPROFILE%\.ssh\known_hosts; the servers connected to remembered without their password), Server's
files and This device (A opens a folder or moves a file, X moves a folder, Y deletes on a second press, B goes a
folder up), Transfers (one at a time on a channel of its own, with its percentage and speed; A tries a failed one
again, X clears the finished, Y stops all on a second press) and SSH server (A reads sshd's state, X starts it or
stops it on a second press, Y reads sshd_config), and Settings (what a transfer does, and the log read in the app).
The connection, the transfers and the password rules are the BC250 app's; paths on the server show from the home as
~, and the log keeps no host, user name or path.
